## Alice (example)

```yaml
name: Alice                   # the name used in planning commands
role: backend                 # primary role; must map to a roleAbbreviation
seniority: senior             # junior | mid | senior | staff
velocityFactor: 0.8           # 1.0 = solid mid-level baseline in primary area
                              # 0.8 = 20% faster, 1.5 = 50% slower
allocation: 100               # % of working time available to this team
# hoursPerDay: 6              # optional per-person override of defaults
skills:                       # proficiency 1-5 per work area; areas must
  backend: 5                  # match /Breakdown area labels
  frontend: 2
  database: 4
  infrastructure: 3
  testing: 3
```

Alice is the senior backend engineer and owns the API layer and database
migrations. Strongest on service architecture and performance work. Avoid
assigning her deep frontend styling tasks. Provides review coverage for
all backend changes; key-person risk on anything payments-related.

## Ben (example)

```yaml
name: Ben
role: frontend
seniority: mid
velocityFactor: 1.0
allocation: 80                # 20% of his time goes to another team
skills:
  backend: 2
  frontend: 4
  database: 2
  infrastructure: 2
  testing: 3
```

Ben is a mid-level frontend engineer working across the component library
and app screens. Solid on React and state management. At 80% allocation
to this team; plan his capacity accordingly.

## Carla (example)

```yaml
name: Carla
role: fullstack
seniority: junior
velocityFactor: 1.5
allocation: 100
skills:
  backend: 3
  frontend: 3
  database: 2
  infrastructure: 1
  testing: 3
```

Carla is a junior fullstack engineer ramping up across the stack. Give
her well-scoped items with clear acceptance criteria. Needs review on
database changes; do not assign infrastructure work solo.

